 "circuits": [
  {
   "id": "spst-switch",
   "title": "Power gating with a push-button manual power-on (SPST)",
   "page": 12,
   "description": "The battery feeds a power-management stage whose output is the always-on rail. The TPL5110 runs from that rail with EN/ONE_SHOT tied to it, so it is in timer mode. Its DRV output drives the gate of a P-channel MOSFET that switches the rail through to the microcontroller's VDD; when DRV goes low the microcontroller is powered, and it signals DONE from a GPIO when finished. REXT from DELAY/M_DRV to ground sets the interval. A push-button from the rail to DELAY/M_DRV gives a manual power-on; while it is held, current VDD/REXT flows through REXT.",
   "parts": [
